Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Renames OpenInputBridge's control devices from \\.\interceptionNN to \\.\oibNN, so both
; oib_kbd.sys/oib_mou.sys and the real Interception driver can be installed side by side without
; \Device\interceptionNN / \DosDevices\interceptionNN name collisions (see
; driver/common/driver.c's OibReadConfiguredDeviceNameBase and driver/common/driver.h's
; OIB_DEVICE_NAME_BASE_VALUE_NAME comment).
;
; Takes effect the next time each driver's DriverEntry runs (the value is read once at driver
; load, not per device arrival) -- reboot after importing this, or after each install/reinstall.
;
; To revert to the default "interception" naming, either delete the DeviceNameBase value under
; both keys below (regedit or `reg delete`), or import a .reg that sets it back to "interception".

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\OpenInputBridgeKeyboard\Parameters]
"DeviceNameBase"="oib"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\OpenInputBridgeMouse\Parameters]
"DeviceNameBase"="oib"
